Action: Discuss and plan out logistics. 
    Storage of objects 
    Team finalised plan to store multiple objects at once, complexity concerns raised but agreement if we are unable to realise this idea we will move back to one at a time concept accepted 
    Multiple compartments on the back of robot with small incline on each basket 
    Latch door to let the corresponding ball roll out the robot. 
    Incline to let the objects roll in and out then into boxes 
    Barrell on back of buggy with four compartments that rotate respective to object needed for deposit. 

Arm of robot 
    Most complex part technically and logistically  
    Discussion of how to drop object in correct baskets 
    Add rubber end onto gripper 
    Use current to measure if an object is grabbed from the current output a button is an easier less technical solution although problematic if it gets jammed 
    Simpler arm that lifts object overhead and onto tracks  

Environment 
    Ensure the objects are in correct colour order for drop off to collaborate with the arm 
    Cannot have robot on GRID floor due to dark lines between floor tiles potentially causing confusion.  Wooden panel with black electrical tape can be used instead. 

 Object shape  
    Potentially different size object so they can roll into different buggy bins, spherical. 
    Obstacle and objects differentiated by whether they are on or off the line. 
    Small object harder to detect. 

 Other parts of buggy 
    RGB sensor on side to detect  
    Accelerometer on buggy to detect if it has fallen over. 
    Two separate Arduinos to allow for simultaneous line following and colour detection, convolution concerns raised. 

